# Platform files compiled from library content — regenerate with compilers
# .claude/agents/*.md
# .claude/rules/*.md

# NO .lib/ RULE ON THIS BRANCH — and that is deliberate.
#
# `.lib/` is blocked on dna-platform, because the organization identity is
# .claude/, CLAUDE.md and README.md, and a branch-library mirror has no business
# there. On a PROJECT branch the opposite is true: `.lib/` IS the project's branch
# library, mirrored from library/*/.lib in the project repo, and it must be tracked.
#
# The rule arrived here by a downstream merge from dna-platform and silently made
# every file under .lib/ uncommittable — which is exactly what stopped this team
# from committing. If you merge dna-platform again and this rule comes back, take
# THIS side.
